e\"\n    97→      },\n    98→      {\n    99→        \"quote\": \"Anthropic has been struggling all of 2026 with usage limits and shenanigans around 'peak hour' reduction.\",\n   100→        \"source\": \"HN\",\n   101→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n   102→      },\n   103→      {\n   104→        \"quote\": \"The race is actually between locally optimized rigs with extremely strict context management, and the rest.\",\n   105→        \"source\": \"HN\",\n   106→        \"sentiment\": \"neutral\"\n   107→      }\n   108→    ]\n   109→  },\n   110→  {\n   111→    \"productName\": \"Claude Code\",\n   112→    \"title\": \"Skill and Plugin Security Scanning (Beta)\",\n   113→    \"description\": \"Enterprise plans can now enable automatic security scanning for third-party skills and plugins when uploaded or edited. Helps detect malicious content before deployment.\",\n   114→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   115→    \"url\": \"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12138966-release-notes\",\n   116→    \"date\": \"2026-08-06\",\n   117→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   118→  },\n   119→  {\n   120→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n   121→    \"title\": \"Origin Code Hosting Platform Launch\",\n   122→    \"description\": \"Cursor launched Origin, a new Git hosting platform in early beta for paid plans. Features include hosted codebases with GitHub repo syncing, pull requests with two-way sync, agent integration for code analysis, and app extensions for Vercel, Depot, and Buildkite. Launch coincided with GitHub's 7-hour outage on August 17.\",\n   123→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   124→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog\",\n   125→    \"date\": \"2026-08-17\",\n   126→    \"community_feedback\": [\n   127→      {\n   128→        \"quote\": \"It's like going from bad to worse.\",\n   129→        \"source\": \"HN\",\n   130→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n   131→      },\n   132→      {\n   133→        \"quote\": \"They are doing the easiest part of git hosting and don't even support GitHub Actions yet.\",\n   134→        \"source\": \"HN\",\n   135→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n   136→      }\n   137→    ]\n   138→  },\n   139→  {\n   140→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n   141→    \"title\": \"Cloud Agents with Subscriptions and Custom Modes\",\n   142→    \"description\": \"Cloud agents gained autonomous capabilities to monitor PRs, watch Slack threads, and run scheduled tasks. New features include custom modes with pinned skills, subagents on isolated VMs, /goal command for persistent objectives, and non-interruptive steering for guiding agents.\",\n   143→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   144→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog\",\n   145→    \"date\": \"2026-08-19\",\n   146→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   147→  },\n   148→  {\n   149→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n   150→    \"title\": \"Grok 4.6 Model Release\",\n   151→    \"description\": \"Cursor released Grok 4.6, a new model focused on long-running agents and complex coding tasks. Features include 500K context window, new XHigh reasoning capability, and improved multi-step reasoning with self-checking. Pricing maintained at $2/$6.\",\n   152→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n   153→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/blog/grok-4-6\",\n   154→    \"date\": \"2026-08-14\",\n   155→    \"community_feedback\": [\n   156→      {\n   157→        \"quote\": \"Users reported impressive value overall and strong performance on coding and knowledge tasks.\",\n   158→        \"source\": \"Cursor Forum\",\n   159→        \"sentiment\": \"positive\"\n   160→      },\n   161→      {\n   162→        \"quote\": \"Some users reported bad experiences with the model not solving problems and high token consumption (>15% usage in a single day).\",\n   163→        \"source\": \"Cursor Forum\",\n   164→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n   165→      },\n   166→      {\n   167→        \"quote\": \"Issues with auto-overriding without user approval.\",\n   168→        \"source\": \"Cursor Forum\",\n   169→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n   170→      }\n   171→    ]\n   172→  },\n   173→  {\n   174→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n   175→    \"title\": \"Cloud Agents 3x Faster Startup with Builds\",\n   176→    \"description\": \"Background preparation of development environments reduces startup time to 3x faster. Agents boot from cached environments with cloned repos and installed dependencies. Failed builds don't disrupt operations as agents continue using last successful build.\",\n   177→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   178→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog\",\n   179→    \"date\": \"2026-08-14\",\n   180→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   181→  },\n   182→  {\n   183→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n   184→    \"title\": \"Google Workspace Plugins\",\n   185→    \"description\": \"New plugins enable agents to work across Gmail (search, draft, send), Google Drive (files, folders), and Google Calendar (events, scheduling). Provides direct integration for workflow automation.\",\n   186→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   187→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog\",\n   188→    \"date\": \"2026-08-04\",\n   189→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   190→  },\n   191→  {\n   192→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n   193→    \"title\": \"Cursor Router with Auto Intelligence\",\n   194→    \"description\": \"Cursor Router optimizes model selection with Auto Intelligence and Auto Balance, delivering 68% lower costs for Intelligence mode while maintaining higher satisfaction.\",\n   195→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   196→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog\",\n   197→    \"date\": \"2026-08-06\",\n   198→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   199→  },\n   200→  {\n   201→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n   202→    \"title\": \"Agent Plugins 1.0 Launch\",\n   203→    \"description\": \"GitHub Copilot launched Agent Plugins 1.0 for VS Code, CLI, and the app, enabling portable agent plugins with multi-catalog search. Features include automatic approval via flags, Cursor skill import and sync, and MCP 2026-07-28 protocol support.\",\n   204→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   205→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/label/copilot/\",\n   206→    \"date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   207→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   208→  },\n   209→  {\n   210→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n   211→    \"title\": \"Grok 4.6 Model Integration\",\n   212→    \"description\": \"GitHub Copilot integrated Grok 4.6 model, expanding model choices for users. The model is designed for long-running agents and complex coding tasks with improved multi-step reasoning.\",\n   213→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   214→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/label/copilot/\",\n   215→    \"date\": \"2026-08-14\",\n   216→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   217→  },\n   218→  {\n   219→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n   220→    \"title\": \"Code Review Effort Levels GA\",\n   221→    \"description\": \"Code review effort levels became generally available, providing more granular control over automated code review capabilities. Allows teams to customize review depth and automation.\",\n   222→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   223→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/label/copilot/\",\n   224→    \"date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   225→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   226→  },\n   227→  {\n   228→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n   229→    \"title\": \"Usage Metrics API Expansion\",\n   230→    \"description\": \"Usage metrics API expanded to include agent app activity, providing more detailed insights into how teams are using Copilot across different platforms and workflows.\",\n   231→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   232→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/label/copilot/\",\n   233→    \"date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   234→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   235→  },\n   236→  {\n   237→    \"productName\": \"Devin\",\n   238→    \"title\": \"Devin Coach Suggestions\",\n   239→    \"description\": \"Devin introduced real-time prompt improvement suggestions that surface directly in the session input box, helping users formulate better prompts and improve AI interactions.\",\n   240→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   241→    \"url\": \"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\",\n   242→    \"date\": \"2026-08-14\",\n   243→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   244→  },\n   245→  {\n   246→    \"productName\": \"Devin\",\n   247→    \"title\": \"Side Chats Feature\",\n   248→    \"description\": \"Users can now start conversations anchored to any point in a session to ask questions without interrupting Devin's main work flow, enabling parallel exploration and clarification.\",\n   249→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   250→    \"url\": \"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\",\n   251→    \"date\": \"2026-08-12\",\n   252→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   253→  },\n   254→  {\n   255→    \"productName\": \"Devin\",\n   256→    \"title\": \"Automations Queueing Support\",\n   257→    \"description\": \"Automations now support queueing with configurable maximum concurrent runs and queue depth. Users can view queue lifecycle states and manage execution flow more effectively.\",\n   258→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   259→    \"url\": \"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\",\n   260→    \"date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   261→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   262→  },\n   263→  {\n   264→    \"productName\": \"Devin\",\n   265→    \"title\": \"Security Profiles GA\",\n   266→    \"description\": \"Security profiles became generally available, allowing admins to define profiles governing network access across sessions and automations for improved security control.\",\n   267→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   268→    \"url\": \"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\",\n   269→    \"date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   270→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   271→  },\n   272→  {\n   273→    \"productName\": \"Devin\",\n   274→    \"title\": \"GitLab Support for Automations\",\n   275→    \"description\": \"Devin Automations now support GitLab triggers and service-account connections, expanding beyond GitHub to support more development workflows.\",\n   276→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   277→    \"url\": \"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\",\n   278→    \"date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   279→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   280→  },\n   281→  {\n   282→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n   283→    \"title\": \"Portable Agent Plugins\",\n   284→    \"description\": \"Codex CLI 0.147.0 introduced Portable Agent Plugins with multi-catalog search, Cursor skill import and sync, and automatic approval via flags. Enhanced secret redaction and improved terminal responsiveness.\",\n   285→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   286→    \"url\": \"https://www.codex-docs.com/en/docs/changelog\",\n   287→    \"date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   288→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   289→  },\n   290→  {\n   291→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n   292→    \"title\": \"Linux Desktop App Preview\",\n   293→    \"description\": \"OpenAI Codex released Linux desktop app preview for Ubuntu, Debian, and Fedora distributions. Added import functionality for Claude Code, Claude Cowork, and Cursor configurations.\",\n   294→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n   295→    \"url\": \"https://www.codex-docs.com/en/docs/changelog\",\n   296→    \"date\": \"2026-08-11\",\n   297→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   298→  },\n   299→  {\n   300→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n   301→    \"title\": \"Computer History Feature\",\n   302→    \"description\": \"Computer History launched as an opt-in feature for macOS desktop app, converting app and website activity into memories and timeline data for improved context awareness.\",\n   303→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   304→    \"url\": \"https://www.codex-docs.com/en/docs/changelog\",\n   305→    \"date\": \"2026-08-13\",\n   306→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   307→  },\n   308→  {\n   309→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n   310→    \"title\": \"Daybreak Cyber Tier Launch\",\n   311→    \"description\": \"Codex introduced Daybreak with two access tiers: 'Daybreak Blue' for general security work and 'Daybreak Red' for specialized cyber operations powered by GPT-5.6 Cyber model.\",\n   312→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   313→    \"url\": \"https://www.codex-docs.com/en/docs/changelog\",\n   314→    \"date\": \"2026-08-10\",\n   315→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   316→  },\n   317→  {\n   318→    \"productName\": \"Gemini CLI\",\n   319→    \"title\": \"PR Generation and Antigravity Agent\",\n   320→    \"description\": \"Gemini CLI v0.55.1 introduced comprehensive PR generation capabilities with Firestore concurrency dual-locking and the Antigravity agent runner with comprehensive prompt templates.\",\n   321→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   322→    \"url\": \"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/latest/\",\n   323→    \"date\": \"2026-08-11\",\n   324→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   325→  },\n   326→  {\n   327→    \"productName\": \"Gemini CLI\",\n   328→    \"title\": \"Enhanced Authentication and Security\",\n   329→    \"description\": \"Implemented strict HTTPS validation for GoogleCredentialsAuthProvider to block cleartext leakage, added tag length validation for file keychain system, and improved caretaker triage loop with descriptive comments.\",\n   330→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   331→    \"url\": \"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/latest/\",\n   332→    \"date\": \"2026-08-11\",\n   333→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   334→  }\n   335→]\n   336→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
